# Cmd+F finds text inside the open thread and counts the matches.
#
# The sidebar's search finds THREADS; nothing found a line inside the one you
# are reading. Opened through the state knob because the harness cannot press
# a Cmd chord (afterhours_gaps.md #49); the buttons and the tally are driven
# for real, by NAME rather than by coordinate so a layout change retargets the
# click instead of quietly landing on empty space.
#
# settings: {"window_width":1100,"window_height":760,"open_tabs":["t2"],"active_tab":"t2","theme":"dark"}
# env: HANABI_FIND_DEMO=ledger

# "ledger" is paintable three times in this thread: the user turn that opens
# it and the two account lines in the first reply. It used to be twice — the
# opening line was a System caption, which has no highlight path and so was
# never counted. That line is a real user message now (the transcript opens on
# a user turn, to match Puffin's), and a user bubble paints like any other, so
# the third occurrence counts. Every counted match is one find would paint, and
# this thread fits the window, so here the tally and the bands are equal
# outright (see find_counts_only_what_it_could_paint.e2e, and
# find_counts_the_thread_not_the_window.e2e for the case where they are not).
expect_text "1 of 3"

# Next advances, and wraps at the end.
click_ui find_next
wait_frames 6
expect_text "2 of 3"
click_ui find_next
wait_frames 6
expect_text "3 of 3"
click_ui find_next
wait_frames 6
expect_text "1 of 3"

# Previous goes the other way, wrapping backwards.
click_ui find_prev
wait_frames 6
expect_text "3 of 3"

# Closing puts the bar away.
click_ui find_close
wait_frames 8
expect_no_text matches
